Note on validation intent: the fast path preserves every required mapping fact per ASCII unit (output byte equals the unit, both unit boundaries valid, `byteToUnit` gains the ending unit offset, byte boundary valid, newline line-start entries added), falls through to the unchanged general path at any non-ASCII unit (preserving BMP runes, surrogate pairs, and unpaired-surrogate replacement), and adds no new allocations, keeping allocation count at eight while materially reducing repeated-ASCII work (no `decodeUTF16Rune`, no `utf8.EncodeRune` per unit).